agent-ops task task-c5e623bf-3720-4980-bf4d-16c12b7a4dae: Surface: cap included globs and surface skipped queries to reviewers
intent: Cap included/unknown globs at 10 tracked files outside the diff (SURFACE_INCLUSION_TOO_BROAD); count derived-query skip threshold outside the diff only; sort skipped ascending and name it in the round-2 prompt with 3 extra grep queries; update en/zh-TW spec, CHANGELOG, surface checks.
criteria:
- inclusion-cap: When one included or unknown path glob matches more than 10 tracked files outside the diff, runSurfaceGate returns NOT_RUN SURFACE_INCLUSION_TOO_BROAD naming the glob and its outside count, and agent-ops review on such a task returns NOT_RUN with reason surface-inclusion-too-broad; a glob matching 10 or fewer outside files passes; proven by tests/surface/surface-checks.mjs under npm test.
- skip-outside-diff: A derived query is skipped only when its hit files outside the diff exceed 10, and each skipped row's files equals that outside count. A token present in 8 changed files plus 3 unlisted siblings makes runSurfaceGate return NOT_RUN SURFACE_UNCLASSIFIED whose details list exactly those 3 sibling paths; proven by a surface check under npm test. A token with 1 changed file and 11 outside files is skipped with files 11 and blocks nothing.
- reviewer-skipped: The reviewer packet's discovery.skipped keeps the first 50 rows after sorting by outside-diff hit count ascending, ties broken by query string ascending. When it is non-empty the round-2 prompt names each skipped query with its count and allows at most 3 extra git grep -F queries in total over them, beyond the per-axis budget (a prompt budget, like the per-axis one); when it is empty that sentence is absent; the round-1 prompt is unchanged. Proven by a surface check under npm test.
- spec-docs: en and zh-TW EVIDENCE-SURFACE-001 document SURFACE_INCLUSION_TOO_BROAD and the outside-diff skip threshold, en and zh-TW REVIEW-ADVERSARIAL-001 document the round-2 skipped budget, CHANGELOG has an Unreleased entry, and the spec token check includes SURFACE_INCLUSION_TOO_BROAD under npm test.
